Algorithm

Step 1: Start the program.
Step 2: Initialize the AVL tree root as NULL.
Step 3: Accept integers from the user and insert them into the AVL tree.
Step 4: Calculate the height and balance factor of each node.
Step 5: Perform the appropriate AVL rotation if the tree becomes unbalanced.
Step 6: Display a menu containing the following options:
Display all traversals.
Insert additional values.
Verify inorder sorted order.
Exit.
Step 7: If the user selects Display Traversals, perform inorder, preorder, postorder, and level-order traversals and display each node with its balance factor.
Step 8: If the user selects Insert Additional Values, accept new integers, insert them into the existing AVL tree, and rebalance the tree whenever required.
Step 9: If the user selects Verify Inorder, check whether the inorder traversal is sorted. Display PASS if sorted; otherwise, display FAIL.
Step 10: Repeat the menu until the user selects Exit.
Step 11: Stop the program.
